{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"special factorization special factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md","fileName":"Special Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Special Factorization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Factoring and Algebraic Identities]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"special factorization special factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md","fileName":"Special Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Special Factorization","heading":"Special Factorization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A special factorization recognizes a polynomial as one side of a standard algebraic identity. Common patterns include a difference of squares, a perfect-square trinomial, and sums or differences of cubes.\n\nRecognition can shorten work and reveal further factors. For example,\n\n$$x^4-81=(x^2-9)(x^2+9)=(x-3)(x+3)(x^2+9).$$\n\nThe first identity exposes another difference of squares, so factorization continues in stages. A pattern should be verified against all signs and exponents rather than applied from visual resemblance alone.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"special factorization special factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Special Factorization.md","fileName":"Special Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Special Factorization","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}